interaction membership-forwards-as-a-relation-not-a-grant
  source human-community-body
  destination address-plane
  relation candidate_lowering
  preserves the published membership's community, member subject, role and state, and a dependency edge on the community body and on the membership's authority reference
  drops the authority reference as a coordinate: it is carried as a dependency so an authority publish retires the cut, and never as a term the plane could match on
  forbidden_inference a membership surviving the cut -> authority, disclosure or entitlement; relationship ownership, capability availability and downstream authority are separate facts
  forbidden_inference a role term -> a permission that role is assumed to carry
  invalidates_on the membership, its community body, or its referenced authority is published (reheat)
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh (no authority coordinate reaches the membership; the community and role coordinates do)
  binding cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c

interaction policy-shape-cuts-before-the-evaluator-decides
  source information-policy
  destination address-plane
  relation candidate_lowering
  preserves the declared shape of a disclosure policy -- one candidate per subject kind and audience, carrying the fields that audience is declared to be able to see and the profile's evidence requirements
  drops every decision: the withheld field and its reason, aggregation floors, evidence release, and the per-request evaluation itself
  forbidden_inference a field term -> a disclosure; the exact evaluator still decides and still returns withheld fields marked with their reason
  forbidden_inference a field absent from an audience's candidate -> the field being empty or the subject not existing; absence is default-deny, the same direction the evaluator defaults
  forbidden_inference an audience coordinate arriving -> the caller being that audience; audience is still supplied by the caller rather than derived from the arriving territory
  invalidates_on the profile declaration is published (reheat)
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh (the parcel owner mailing address is unreachable as the public and reachable as an institution)
  binding cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c

interaction spatial-narrows-coarsely-and-stops
  source spatial-observation
  destination address-plane
  relation candidate_lowering
  preserves whether a subject is spatially participating at all, its mobility phenotype, scale band, region, coarse cell, geometry kind, and the mode by which its position was arrived at
  drops the geometry, the CRS and the datum; every exact spatial predicate -- intersects, contains, within-radius, along-route, nearest-N, visible-from, reachable-from -- stays with the spatial owner and runs on the survivors
  forbidden_inference two subjects sharing a coarse cell -> those subjects being near each other
  forbidden_inference a spatial candidate surviving the cut -> a spatial relationship holding; the cut removes what cannot possibly be related and computes nothing
  forbidden_inference a coarse coordinate -> a location precise enough to act on
  invalidates_on the observation, or any observation it was derived from, is published (reheat)
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh (a cell and a mobility phenotype select the population; no geometry or CRS reaches the plane as a term)
  binding cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c

interaction a-derived-position-is-not-an-observation
  source spatial-observation
  destination occurrence-spine
  relation derivation_typing
  preserves the observation mode on every position and the references from a derived position back to the fixes it was computed from
  drops nothing; a derived position is recorded rather than discarded, because interpolation is legitimate and only its promotion to observation is not
  forbidden_inference an interpolated, propagated or simulated position -> an observation a source made
  forbidden_inference a derived position being wrong later -> the observations under it being wrong; the fixes are append-only and the derivation is what gets recomputed
  forbidden_inference a fast-moving projection -> history being written at that rate
  invalidates_on any observation named in derived_from is published or retracted (reheat)
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh (asking for what a source observed never returns the interpolation between two fixes, and asking for the interpolation never returns the fixes)
  binding cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c

interaction coverage-is-reach-not-entitlement
  source coverage-volume
  destination information-policy
  relation separate_decision
  preserves the coverage volume's owner, derivation, quality, scale and coarse position as a statement about reach
  drops any suggestion that reach settles disclosure; what may be told about a subject inside a coverage volume is decided per field and per audience by the evaluator, unchanged
  forbidden_inference a camera covering a place -> footage of that place being lawful to hold, publish or search
  forbidden_inference a delivery or service radius reaching a subject -> that subject being entitled to the service
  forbidden_inference a specified coverage -> a measured one
  invalidates_on the coverage declaration or the governing policy declaration is published (reheat)
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh (a coverage volume carries no authority, audience or field coordinate, and a specified footprint is not returned when asking for a measured one)
  binding cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c

interaction reconstruction-is-recomputed-not-replayed
  source spatial-observation
  destination occurrence-spine
  relation bitemporal_reconstruction
  preserves both time axes on every fact -- when a source saw a position, when that position is claimed to hold, when it expires, and when this estate learned it -- and every retraction as an appended fact with its own knowledge time
  drops nothing; the log is append-only and a correction is an addition, so the state at any earlier knowledge frontier remains computable rather than remembered
  forbidden_inference a reconstruction -> a recording; nothing replays a stored frame and the answer is recomputed from facts at a stated frontier pair
  forbidden_inference a position being the latest known -> that position being current; a claim past valid_until expires and expiry is reported distinctly from never having observed the subject
  forbidden_inference a retraction -> the retracted fact never having been believed; what was believed at an earlier knowledge time stays reproducible, which is the whole reason retraction appends
  forbidden_inference a derived position outliving a retracted basis -> that position still standing; it is marked as an orphaned derivation
  invalidates_on any fact for the subject, or a retraction of one, is appended (reheat)
  witness cmd/BonfyreSpatial/tests/spatial_test.sh (one valid instant answers differently at two knowledge times; UPDATE and DELETE abort at the store)
  binding cmd/BonfyreSpatial/src/main.c

interaction exact-closure-runs-on-what-the-plane-left
  source address-plane
  destination spatial-observation
  relation exact_verification
  preserves the coarse cut's surviving population, and the frontier the question was asked at
  drops the plane's role entirely at this point: the mask said what could not possibly participate, and every distance, containment and ordering decision here is computed exactly from geometry the plane never saw
  forbidden_inference surviving the coarse cut -> being within any radius, box or route; the cut removes impossibilities and asserts no proximity
  forbidden_inference a subject being returned by the closure -> that subject's position being disclosable to the asker; InformationPolicy decides that separately and afterwards
  forbidden_inference a nearest-N result -> a complete answer over subjects this estate has never observed
  invalidates_on the compiled advertisement generation is replaced, or a fact at the frontier is appended (reheat)
  witness cmd/BonfyreSpatial/tests/spatial_test.sh (each subject contributes one position per frontier; a measured haversine separation of 0.009 degrees latitude lands between 995 and 1010 metres)
  binding cmd/BonfyreSpatial/src/main.c

interaction the-frontier-travels-and-the-population-does-not
  source spatial-observation
  destination web-address-edge
  relation projection_addressing
  preserves the frontier pair -- the valid instant and the knowledge instant -- plus extent, region, cell and an optional subject of interest, all as projection coordinates in the address itself
  drops the population entirely; no subject, position, geometry or layer content is serialised, so the recipient recompiles the closure under their own actor and policy
  forbidden_inference holding an address -> access to what it projects; a link grants nothing the recipient could not have asked for themselves
  forbidden_inference a subject named in an address -> that subject existing, being observed, or being disclosable to the holder
  forbidden_inference two people opening one address -> two people seeing the same thing; they see the same frontier resolved under different closures, and that is the intended behaviour
  invalidates_on nothing; an address is a pure function of its coordinates and holds no state to invalidate
  witness cmd/BonfyreSpatial/tests/spatial_test.sh (the rendered address round-trips exactly, carries no subject or geometry, and is refused when it carries no frontier, a malformed instant or an undeclared coordinate)
