interaction a-receipted-observation-becomes-a-position
  source foreign-twin
  destination spatial-observation
  relation intake_mapping
  preserves the source's own instant, the occurrence and digest that identify the document observed, and the subject key the source published, under a mapping declared per source rather than inferred from the payload
  drops every feature the mapping cannot place honestly -- no source instant, a geometry this owner cannot place exactly, no subject key, or a source instant later than the moment of ingest -- each refused and counted separately rather than dropped quietly
  forbidden_inference a feature carrying no instant -> an observation at the moment of ingest; a stamped feature is indistinguishable from a real one forever afterwards, so it is refused instead
  forbidden_inference an ingested position -> an admitted, disclosable or authoritative one; intake records what a source said and settles nothing about whether it may be repeated
  forbidden_inference observing one document twice -> two observations; ingest is idempotent by the whole source digest
  forbidden_inference an empty ingest -> a source that reported nothing; an unparseable document fails rather than recording an absence
  invalidates_on the source is re-observed and a new receipt with a different digest arrives (reheat)
