  drops the temptation to store a representative point for an extent; there is none, so distance is computed against the shape and containment is answered by the shape
  forbidden_inference a bounding box overlapping -> the shapes overlapping; a box is a rejection and never an answer
  forbidden_inference a distance to an extent -> a distance to its centre; the two differ by the size of the thing and differ most where it is largest
  forbidden_inference a point inside an area's outer ring -> a point inside the area; a hole subtracts, and a courtyard is not the building
  invalidates_on a fact for the subject is appended (reheat)
